data: {"type": "final", "payload": "**审慎结论：该论断得到\"部分支持\"——RAG 在多数情况下能降低幻觉风险，但并非无条件成立，检索质量不佳时反而可能加剧幻觉。**\n\n证据立场统计显示：支持 2 条、反驳 0 条、中立 4 条，整体判定为\"部分支持\"。具体依据如下：\n\n**支持面（RAG 确实有助于降低幻觉）**\n- 《Retrieval-Augmented Generation》(2025) 指出 RAG 将大模型的生成能力与信息检索系统的事实可靠性相结合，隐含了降低幻觉的作用。\n- 《Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Enhancing AI with Reliable Knowledge》(2025) 表明 RAG 用于解决模型输出不准确或过时的问题，隐含降低幻觉。\n- 检索到的其他文献也印证了这一方向：如《Coarse-to-Fine Highlighting: Reducing Knowledge Hallucination in Large Language Models》(2024) 明确以\"减少知识幻觉\"为目标；《\"Knowing When You Don't Know\": A Multilingual Relevance Assessment Dataset for Robust Retrieval-Augmented Generation》(2023) 指出 RAG 通过外部知识源\"grounding\"来减少事实幻觉。\n\n**审慎之处（RAG 并非万能，存在条件性）**\n- 《Removal of Hallucination on Hallucination: Debate-Augmented RAG》(2025) 提出了关键反例：当检索结果本身错误或有偏时，RAG 会把错误知识引入生成，反而\"复合\"幻觉（作者称之为\"Hallucination on Hallucination\"）。这说明 RAG 降低幻觉的效果高度依赖检索质量。\n- 多篇证据（如《Layered Query Retrieval...》(2024)）只强调 RAG 解决知识截止和模型固有局限，并未直接、明确地量化\"幻觉风险降低\"这一结论。\n\n**综合判断**：RAG 通过引入外部知识源为模型输出提供\"grounding\"，在检索质量可靠的前提下确实能显著降低幻觉风险，这是该领域的主流共识；但这一效果是有条件的——检索错误、检索内容有偏或与问题不匹配时，RAG 不仅不能降低幻觉，反而可能放大它。因此更准确的表述是：**RAG 能降低幻觉风险，但前提是检索环节可靠**，不能把\"RAG 必然降低幻觉\"当作无条件成立的结论。", "meta": {"runtime": "langgraph", "node": "reflect", "phase": "自检修正", "elapsed_ms": 884, "session_id": "a04a-success-20260810", "stop_reason": "completed", "tokens_in": 5589, "tokens_out": 480, "structured_answer": {"schema_version": "answer-contract/v1", "capability": "claim_verification", "status": "partially_supported", "verdict_label": "部分支持", "answer_mode": "evidence_based", "citation_compliance": "ok", "citations": [{"paper_id": "W4412945185", "title": "Removal of Hallucination on Hallucination: Debate-Augmented RAG", "year": 2025, "chunk_uid": "2c1110850f13777c191fcebbf706014ceb9e1407", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "Retrieval-Augmented Generation (RAG) enhances factual accuracy by integrating external knowledge, yet it introduces a critical issue: erroneous or biased retrieval can mislead generation, compounding hallucinations, a phenomenon we term Hallucination on Hallucination.", "stance": "NEUTRAL", "confidence": 0.5}, {"paper_id": "W4416075695", "title": "Retrieval-Augmented Generation", "year": 2025, "chunk_uid": "330e7c65b696a4fed024bab69d7a3aee262c4815", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) is a hybrid architecture that combines the generative power of large language models (LLMs) with the factual reliability of information retrieval systems.", "stance": "SUPPORT", "confidence": 0.6}, {"paper_id": "W4416026024", "title": "Retrieval-Augmented Generation: Enhancing AI with Reliable Knowledge.", "year": 2025, "chunk_uid": "b1cd58b0261e45af5bdffca3d28107f7d0ff16b5", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "", "stance": "NEUTRAL", "confidence": 0.0}, {"paper_id": "W4404765644", "title": "Layered Query Retrieval: An Adaptive Framework for Retrieval-Augmented Generation in Complex Question Answering for Large Language Models", "year": 2024, "chunk_uid": "c08265569014211895a92ac420c8c23a1a3bcd36", "source_field": "abstract", "evidence_sentence": "Retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) addresses the problem of knowledge cutoff and overcomes the inherent limitations of pre-trained language models by retrieving relevant information in real time.", "stance": "NEUTRAL", "confidence": 0.5}], "uncertainty": {"category": "none", "message": "", "calibrated_rejection": false, "qualification_hints": ["证据指出RAG可能加剧幻觉，而非降低幻觉风险，与论断方向相反但未明确否定整体降低作用。", "证据强调事实可靠性，但未直接提及幻觉风险降低。", "证据表明RAG解决不准确或过时响应问题，隐含降低幻觉，但未明确使用'幻觉'一词。", "证据关注知识截止和模型局限，未直接提及幻觉风险。", "证据提及RAG可解决幻觉问题，但句子不完整，置信度略低。"]}, "tool_basis": ["verify_claim"], "claim": "检索增强生成（RAG）能够降低大语言模型回答中的幻觉风险"}}}

data: [DONE]

